*** docs/skills/repository-operations.md (proposed beside finite archive budgets and exact physical aliases)
+Budget every simultaneously retained compressed copy. A same-filesystem
+exclusive hardlink promotion may avoid a second data copy only after complete
+staging verification and durable indices; fsync the destination and its directory
+before unlinking the staged name. Preserve both names on an earlier failure.
+Relocating a failed partial preserves its exact bytes and metadata, not gzip
+completion. Keep the original failure and original path in a separately typed
+physical alias, and validate that plan before any file mutation.
